# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data policy
#
# Tracked (LFS):   only what no script can produce.
#   src/data/fornlamningar_full.gpkg   the RAA export; seeds the crawl
#   src/data/signs/                    Kungsbacka's sign layer (a dead end,
#                                      kept as the evidence for that)
#   hand_labels.csv                    the only ground truth not derived
#                                      from documentation
#
# Ignored:         everything below. Two kinds, both left out of git but for
#                  different reasons.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. CACHES. Regenerable, but only by hitting a network service again, so they
#    are worth keeping on disk indefinitely. ksamsok_raw is 4 hours of
#    rate-limited crawling (311,845 responses); re-fetching it to save 1.3 GB
#    of local disk would be a bad trade.
src/data/ksamsok_raw.sqlite
# By pattern, not per file. These were listed one database at a time, so
# descriptions.sqlite-wal and -shm were not covered and turned up as
# untracked noise the moment that database existed.
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
src/data/osm/
src/data/wikidata_cache/
# Same bucket, same reasoning. Both are network caches with real cost behind
# them: wikimedia is ~4,000 API calls (1,881 article extracts, 1,877 pageview
# series, 2,000+ Commons files) and lansstyrelsen is a CSW sweep plus 26
# geodata downloads, 267 web pages and two PDFs. Cheap to re-run, rude to
# re-run casually.
src/data/wikimedia.sqlite
src/data/lansstyrelsen.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
# The RAA archaeological-assignment extracts: 192 MB of GeoPackage, one
# download from pub.raa.se, no account needed.
src/data/raa/

# 2. DERIVED. Pure functions of the tracked inputs plus the caches above.
#    `./run_pipeline.sh` rebuilds all of it in ~4 minutes, so committing it
#    would only mean a 700 MB LFS object going stale on every rerun.
src/data/sites.sqlite
src/data/tiles_input.geojsonl
# One table of everything anyone has written about a place, assembled from
# sites.sqlite + the two caches above by build_sources.py. 473 MB of text we
# already have in three other files.
src/data/sources.sqlite
src/data/labels.sqlite

# Review samples: output of sample_for_review.py. The verdicts they collect
# live in hand_labels.csv, which IS tracked; the sample sheets themselves are
# scratch.
review_*.csv
